text:
maria_docs: Quick thread  we need a concise docs blurb for UK data residency (including a tiny curl + JS snippet). Theres some nuance for Northern Ireland and post-Brexit routing; can someone help draft wording and code?

leigh_l10n: I can draft. Do we use `X-Region: uk` for examples? Any preference for showing NI explicitly?

sam_platform: Use `X-Region: uk` as the canonical example. Internally we may normalize and map requests (e.g., `uk-ni` when routed specifically to Northern Ireland infra) and we emit `x-region-declared` + `x-region-routed` headers. Note: header values are lowercase.

leigh_l10n: Drafting snippets now. Keeping them minimal: 

```bash
# curl example
curl -sS https://api.redwoodinference.com/v1/generate \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" \
  -H "X-Region: uk" \
  -d '{"model":"redwood-1-small","prompt":"Hello from the UK"}'
```

```js
// Node SDK illustrative example
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });
const res = await client.generate({
  model: 'redwood-1-small',
  prompt: 'Hello from the UK',
  headers: { 'X-Region': 'uk' }
});
// detect if request was routed elsewhere
if (res.headers && res.headers['x-region-routed'] && res.headers['x-region-routed'] !== 'uk') {
  console.warn('Routed to fallback region:', res.headers['x-region-routed']);
}
console.log(res.text);
```

emma_legal: Suggested legal blurb: "Requests targeted to the United Kingdom are processed under UK jurisdiction and data handling practices; please consult your agreement for binding residency guarantees." Keep it high level and non-binding.

maria_docs: Good. Can we add one short sentence clarifying NI nuance: "In some cases, requests may be handled in Northern Ireland infrastructure (value `uk-ni`) or nearby EU/UK regions depending on availability and settings."

sam_platform: Confirmed. We will surface the final routing in `x-region-routed` and the Console Request logs. For customers using strict residency (Private/Dedicated) we attempt to honor the requested region; otherwise hosting/availability may cause fallback. We'll add a note in the docs to check Console logs for the final region.

leigh_l10n: I'll open a PR with the curl + JS snippets, the two-line residency note, and a short Console hint. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/2129 (draft).

docs-bot: docs CI: preview build queued for PR #2129

maria_docs: Quick copy edit (US English) and then merge. Also add a TODO to include a small migration note for customers moving endpoints to `uk` region.

emma_legal: LGTM after the copy-edit. Keeping legal line as-is.

leigh_l10n: Pushed edits for US style. CI passed: docs-bot: preview build success ✅

maria_docs: Merged to staging and promoted to preview. Adding a TODO in the PR to follow up on migration guidance and telemetry for region audit logs.

sam_platform: We'll track the audit flag in infra backlog. No doc changes needed now.

maria_docs: Thanks all  closing the thread.
